Team,

Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

A customer dispute cannot be assessed from the complaint text alone because a=
uthorisation, posting, reversal and contact dates differ. The possible storie=
s are that the complaint outcome does not match the underlying evidence, that=
 a bank-side delay caused the loss, or that the customer saw a temporary post=
ing as final.

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use July 2023 as the new evidence point rather t=
han recycling the earlier conclusion. Several teams are reporting more failed=
 or retried activity than they expected, but they do not agree on the cause.

Please prepare a one-page finding note plus the underlying CSV for our own re=
view. The output must help us decide the evidence position and whether remedi=
ation should precede correspondence.

Data available: transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts, statuses and=
 error context; customer contacts, complaints and suggestions; ATM attempts, =
host responses, PIN attempts, blocked-card state and latency.

Please state the limitation plainly: Use statements only where they exist and=
 do not invent merchant evidence or call recordings.

